 "summary": "Establishes certain renunciations shall not necessarily constitute a qualified disclaimer for the purposes of the estate tax or the gift tax; allows a beneficiary of a disposition to renounce certain portions of his or her portion of an interest in joint property or tenancy by the entirety; allows a renouncing party to file a copy of a renunciation and affidavit in the office of the clerk of the court having jurisdiction; relates to who may make a renunciation.",
